title: Coworker
---

//Setting up the scene
// <<ChangeLocation DialogueSignals "Hallway">> -----> This is the command to set the player to a specific location, and isn't needed here

//<<SetCharacterLocation DialogueSignals "Scarlet" "Hallway">> ----> this is already set at the end of the previous node


Scarlet:Hey {$name}! How's it going? !#expression:happy #pose:normal
{$name}:Oh hey Scarlet.
{$name}:I'm doing okay. Can't wait for lunch though. You?
Scarlet:Ugh, tell me about it. Heard the canteens selling some sort of 'pasta surprise' today. Me personally? I'll stick with bringing my own food.#expression:normal
{$name}:Oh yeah, for sure. Screw that 'surprise' nonsense, we all know it's last weeks leftovers.
Scarlet:Speaking of leftovers, heard you got last pick for shifts this week. Working the Spice ward? Yikes!#expression:sus
{$name}:Yeah, but it's not been too bad so far. A bit of a slow week, actually.
Scarlet:Have you met the new one? C-50-093? That freaky ass pink chick?#expression:normal
{$name}:Who, Cherry?
Scarlet:Cherry?! It has a name!?#expression:sus
{$name}:It? I'm pretty sure she's a she!
Scarlet:Damn. Well I guess that means you've met it, or her, or whatever. What's she like?#expression:normal
-> Truth
    {$name}:She's kinda cool. She's not super friendly or anything, but at least she actually talks to me. Most of the others just growl or scream or whatever. She's quite... chill, comparatively.
-> Lie
    {$name}:Ugh. She's so annoying and hard to talk to. I wouldn't recommend talking to her, at all.
Scarlet:Wack. How are you not, like, fully scared of her? I would be petrified, especially since she killed all those people.#expression:sus
{$name}:Wait, what? What people?
Scarlet:The Dark Matter explosion? Like a week ago?#expression:sus
{$name}:That was her??
Scarlet:Uh, yeah? Did you not realise? Dumbass
{$name}:Woah. Well, guess I've got something to talk about next time I see her.
Scarlet:Guess so. Shoot, better get back to my rounds before I get yelled at. See you at lunch?#expression:normal
{$name}:Yeah. See you.

<<RemoveCharacter DialogueSignals "Scarlet">>
<<jump EndDay>>
